I have identified the root cause and prepared a fix.

## Root Cause
`binaryToComparableString` uses `String.fromCharCode.apply(String, largeArray)`, which passes each byte as a separate argument. JavaScript engines cap the number of allowed arguments, causing `RangeError` for large buffers (e.g., 200,000 bytes).

## Fix
Process the buffer in chunks of 65,536 bytes (well below the engine limit) to avoid the argument cap. Small buffers still use the fast path.

```javascript
export default function binaryToComparableString(view) {
  const uint8 = new Uint8Array(view.buffer, view.byteOffset, view.byteLength);

  // Fast path for small buffers (<= 65k)
  if (uint8.length <= 65536) {
    return String.fromCharCode.apply(String, uint8);
  }

  // Chunked path for large buffers
  const CHUNK_SIZE = 65536;
  let result = '';

  for (let i = 0; i < uint8.length; i += CHUNK_SIZE) {
    const chunk = uint8.slice(i, Math.min(i + CHUNK_SIZE, uint8.length));
    result += String.fromCharCode.apply(String, chunk);
  }

  return result;
}
